  <p>Look at the fourth row. Meta publishes no pixel size for an ordinary photo on a page, in its Help Center or in its developer pages. The 1,080 by 1,350 that fills most size guides is 4:5 worked out at 1,080 pixels wide, not a Facebook figure. Meta's own number for that shape is the ads guide's 1,440 by 1,800.</p>

  <h2>How do organic page posts and ads differ?</h2>

  <p>The ad side is roomier on almost every line. A post that a tool publishes to a page runs on Meta's developer limits, which are tighter. A post made by hand in the app often has no published limit at all.</p>

